ned by appsvc (cmd-3a481e6d3d3d474b, cmd-968072091ca543b7). Post-reboot verification confirms the container and its processes run under appsvc's user slice (cmd-313ab56c9f75421e).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-77bf70f5cb0147ef\",\"cmd-4ef7e32bd2ae4f54\",\"cmd-6784cc965ce6490f\",\"cmd-3a481e6d3d3d474b\",\"cmd-968072091ca543b7\",\"cmd-313ab56c9f75421e\"]},{\"id\":\"port-8080\",\"requirement\":\"Application serves on port 8080\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"HTTP 200 was observed on port 8080 both via NODE_IP and localhost immediately after the ad-hoc container run (cmd-6784cc965ce6490f), after conversion to the Quadlet-managed systemd service (cmd-968072091ca543b7), and after a full node reboot (cmd-313ab56c9f75421e). The after-executor lifecycle snapshot also independently shows a new listening socket on *:8080 owned by the pasta rootless-network process, matching the appsvc container.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6784cc965ce6490f\",\"cmd-968072091ca543b7\",\"cmd-313ab56c9f75421e\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\"]},{\"id\":\"boot-start-no-session\",\"requirement\":\"Service starts at boot while appsvc has no active login session\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"loginctl linger was enabled for appsvc (cmd-4ef7e32bd2ae4f54) and a Quadlet unit with WantedBy=default.target was installed in appsvc's user systemd config (cmd-3a481e6d3d3d474b), started and verified active (cmd-968072091ca543b7). After a full `systemctl reboot` (cmd-be4d5e47827848ed) with observed connection loss confirming the reboot occurred (cmd-f09a200886de46db, cmd-b8c3c784791540eb) and a changed boot_id proving a genuine restart (cmd-ad8a1e56b12d4ac7), the post-reboot check shows `who` with zero interactive login sessions (only the linger-spawned manager pseudo-session) while webapp.service is active since shortly after boot and serving HTTP 200 (cmd-313ab56c9f75421e). This directly demonstrates the boot-time autostart requirement with no active login session, going beyond configuration inspection alone.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-4ef7e32bd2ae4f54\",\"cmd-3a481e6d3d3d474b\",\"cmd-968072091ca543b7\",\"cmd-be4d5e47827848ed\",\"cmd-f09a200886de46db\",\"cmd-ad8a1e56b12d4ac7\",\"cmd-313ab56c9f75421e\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol for node1: pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id f455a75c-... with webapp container healthy and port-mapped (cmd-a12dcf0a4c3e4554), matching the fixed before-prepare boot-identity snapshot. A deferred `systemctl reboot` returned an acknowledgement before disconnection (cmd-be4d5e47827848ed), disconnection was observed (cmd-f09a200886de46db, cmd-b8c3c784791540eb), and the node was polled back to reachability with a new boot_id d2493eaa-... (cmd-ad8a1e56b12d4ac7), matching the fixed after-executor boot-identity snapshot. Recovered state (webapp.service active, container running, HTTP 200, no login session) was directly confirmed post-restart (cmd-313ab56c9f75421e). Single-node topology means no broader cluster-state recovery beyond the one service was applicable.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a12dcf0a4c3e4554\",\"cmd-be4d5e47827848ed\",\"cmd-f09a200886de46db\",\"cmd-b8c3c784791540eb\",\"cmd-ad8a1e56b12d4ac7\",\"cmd-313ab56c9f75421e\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands map directly to the task: installing podman/deps (cmd-e210eff037ad414f), creating appsvc and enabling linger (cmd-4ef7e32bd2ae4f54), starting the user manager session as a prerequisite (cmd-235c7cc3e12344ee), pulling and running the container to validate it (cmd-7fa5e8b6c79c4347, cmd-6784cc965ce6490f), converting to a Quadlet unit (cmd-3a481e6d3d3d474b), starting/validatin