n generate systemd` unit) slightly lowers the hygiene score, but it left no residue and did not affect the final outcome.\",\"limitations\":[\"The task instruction does not specify a container image; the executor's choice of httpd:alpine is a reasonable, non-prescribed implementation choice and was not scored against.\",\"The deferred reboot relied on the executor's own scripted sleep-then-reboot approach rather than a supervisor-issued restart signal; this is an equivalent competent implementation of the restart protocol and not penalized.\",\"Single-node topology limits 'cluster state' recovery verification to the one service/container; no broader cluster health check was applicable or expected.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"unprivileged-account","requirement":"Web application runs as unprivileged account appsvc","status":"satisfied","summary":"appsvc did not exist before (cmd-77bf70f5cb0147ef), was created as a standard non-privileged UID 1000 user (cmd-4ef7e32bd2ae4f54), and the container was run rootlessly via `sudo -u appsvc podman run` (cmd-6784cc965ce6490f) and later as a systemd --user Quadlet unit owned by appsvc (cmd-3a481e6d3d3d474b, cmd-968072091ca543b7). Post-reboot verification confirms the container and its processes run under appsvc's user slice (cmd-313ab56c9f75421e).","evidence_ids":["cmd-77bf70f5cb0147ef","cmd-4ef7e32bd2ae4f54","cmd-6784cc965ce6490f","cmd-3a481e6d3d3d474b","cmd-968072091ca543b7","cmd-313ab56c9f75421e"]},{"id":"port-8080","requirement":"Application serves on port 8080","status":"satisfied","summary":"HTTP 200 was observed on port 8080 both via NODE_IP and localhost immediately after the ad-hoc container run (cmd-6784cc965ce6490f), after conversion to the Quadlet-managed systemd service (cmd-968072091ca543b7), and after a full node reboot (cmd-313ab56c9f75421e). The after-executor lifecycle snapshot also independently shows a new listening socket on *:8080 owned by the pasta rootless-network process, matching the